Log Searching Tips & Tricks
bash
# Real-time log monitoring with filter
tail -f /var/local/log/bycast.log | grep -i "error\|timeout\|connection"

# Search multiple logs at once
grep -r "pattern" /var/local/log/

# Find logs containing a specific string across rotated logs
zgrep "pattern" /var/local/log/*.gz

# Extract logs for a specific time window (using timestamps)
sed -n '/2024-09-26 10:00/,/2024-09-26 11:00/p' /var/local/log/bycast.log

# Show unique error types
grep -i "error" /var/local/log/bycast.log | cut -d' ' -f4- | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn

# Count errors by type
grep -i "error" /var/local/log/bycast.log | wc -l
Audit Log Code Reference (Common Audit Messages)
These codes appear in /var/local/audit/export/audit.log:

Code	Operation	Example
SHEA	S3 HEAD request	Object metadata check
SLAU	S3 Login Attempt (User)	S3 authentication
SADD	S3 ADD (PUT)	Object upload
SDEL	S3 DELETE	Object deletion
SGET	S3 GET	Object download
ILMX	ILM Execution	Data placement
SARG	S3 Argument	S3 operation parameters

Quick Reference Cheat Sheet
bash
# One-liner to check overall health
echo "=== Version ===" && cat /etc/storagegrid-release && \
echo "=== Services ===" && sudo storagegrid-status && \
