Pro Tips for Support Engineers
Always collect logs first before troubleshooting deeper
Use timestamps from errors to narrow down log searching
Enable tail -f in one terminal while testing in another
Archive logs if they're large (gzip) before downloading
Check audit logs for security/permission issues (they're more detailed than bycast.log)
Use grep with context (-B 5 -A 5) to understand error context
Create support bundle when you need to escalate to NetApp (it includes everything)
